The TypeScript adaptation refuses softclip=1 (atan) and any phase other
than 0 (cos/sin), so the phase rotation runs with native's exact cos(0)=1 and
sin(0)=0 coefficients. It accepts only constant decimal values, the mode and
bmode names or integers and the boolean names or 0/1, refuses inputs native
would remix to stereo implicitly, non-finite input samples and NaN results,
and has no timeline enable or runtime commands. The original source and full
notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
